course: dictionary
lesson: 12383
title: Culled: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Culled» is a verb, a doing word. Its basic idea is to pick something out or remove it from a group. Officials sometimes use it to make a harder word sound softer.
explain: «The council culled the deer to keep their numbers down.» Here culled is a polite, technical word for killed. Ask yourself: what word would fit? Killed fits, so that is the meaning here.
explain: «Mia culled the best facts from three books for her project.» Nobody is hurt in this sentence. The clue is facts from books: culled means chose or picked out from a large group. The context decides the meaning every time.
fact: Culled means killed animals to reduce their numbers, or because they are ill.
fact: Culled also means chose or picked out from a large group.
fact: In business, culled means cut or removed, as in «The company culled 200 jobs.»
fact: Culled is a euphemism: a softer, polite word that hides a harder meaning like killed.
fact: Check the clues: animals or numbers point to killing, while facts or items point to picking out.
exercise: «The farmer culled the sick sheep.» What does culled mean here? | Picked out for a prize | Counted slowly, one by one | Shaved, to keep them cool | *Killed, to reduce the flock or because they are ill
exercise: «Mia culled the best facts from three books.» What does culled mean here? | *Chose, picking out the best from a large group | Printed in bold letters | Burned to ash | Lost by mistake
exercise: Why might an official say «culled» instead of «killed»? | To show that it is a song | It is a longer word | It means exactly the same as killed, so there is no reason to change | *To make a harsh word sound softer and more technical
test: «The company culled 200 jobs last year.» What does culled mean? | Counted twice | *Removed | Hired | Painted
test: Which word is a euphemism, a polite word hiding a harsh meaning, for killed? | Hugged | *Culled | Rescued | Sang
exam: Ruby reads «The ranger culled a few old deer, and the wood was quieter» and guesses culled means picked out for a prize. What do the clues tell her? | Culled means shouted at by the ranger | Ruby is right: culled means picked out for a prize | *Culled here means killed, because the deer are the animals being reduced and the wood is quieter | Culled means lost in the wood
